{"query": "{\"intent\": \"fix: drop overlapping LSP text edits instead of panicking\\n\\nA language server may send overlapping text edits (the LSP spec forbids it,\\nbut some servers do it anyway). `generate_transaction_from_edits` sorted the\\nedits but `ChangeSet::from_changes`, will panic on overlapping ranges.\\n\\nFixes: #15514\"}", "user_id": "85b2e5e0-7745-43f3-8dfe-cff70ebd97f3", "event": "API: Searching code", "logger": "synsc.api.http_server", "level": "info", "timestamp": "2026-09-09T05:54:45.727563Z"}
INFO:     127.0.0.1:51383 - "POST /v1/search/code HTTP/1.1" 200 OK
{"query": "{\"intent\": \"fix: :reload-all, sync all views of a reloaded document\\n\\n`:reload-all` reloads each document by re-reading it from disk and\\ncommitting the diff to history through `view_ids[0]` only. With a split\\nshowing the same document in more than one window, the other views are left\\npointing at the pre-reload revision: their `doc_revisions` and jumplist\\nentries still describe the old (e.g. larger) buffer.\\n\\nA subsequent edit committed through such a stale view runs\\n`append_changes_to_history -> View::apply -> JumpList::apply`, which maps the\\nview's jumplist through a changeset whose pre-image no longer contains those\\npositions, panicking in `ChangeSet::update_positions`:\\n\\n    Positions [(N, ..)] are out of range for changeset len M!\\n\\nSync every view that points at the reloaded document, not just the first, so\\nall of them advance to the post-reload revision and their jumplists are\\nmapped through the reload changeset.\\n\\nFixes: #9830\"}", "user_id": "85b2e5e0-7745-43f3-8dfe-cff70ebd97f3", "event": "API: Searching code", "logger": "synsc.api.http_server", "level": "info", "timestamp": "2026-09-09T05:54:45.813636Z"}
INFO:     127.0.0.1:51383 - "POST /v1/search/code HTTP/1.1" 200 OK
{"query": "{\"intent\": \"fix: track previous mode in insert_at_line_end\\n\\nwe immediately enter insert mode, so that condition always evaluated false.\"}", "user_id": "85b2e5e0-7745-43f3-8dfe-cff70ebd97f3", "event": "API: Searching code", "logger": "synsc.api.http_server", "level": "info", "timestamp": "2026-09-09T05:54:45.951170Z"}
